C. PADS (Rogers PORON 4701-30 Very Soft, 320 kg/m3, 3.18 mm (0.125 in), black (04); standing on the plate in two floor windows 24 x 20, 960 mm2)
   compression: nominal 1.08 (34 %), least 0.36 (13 %, thin pad, unit high), most 1.80 (51 %, thick pad, unit low)
   so the unit always stands on the pads, pressed up against the frame's ledges; at 25 % the sheet gives 21 to 55 kPa, 20 to 53 N
   (the sheet states 25 % only: the preload at the nominal, the least and the most compression is not stated). The unit's bottom at its
   lowest stands 0.10 above the floor top (1.6), the hard stop toward the lid. The pads are compressed by screwing the frame down, not by
   pushing the unit past them. The sheet: constant use to 90 C, compression set 10 % at most at 70 C, so a pad may lose up to 0.18 of its
   compression in storage at +71 C, which the least compression above does not cover: the pads are renewed if T9 finds the unit loose.

D. RETENTION. Unit and mated plugs 0.240 kg (maker's 220 g + 20 g INFERRED): 2.35 N per g. With the tray, frame and plate 0.372 kg.
   LOAD CASE the set is designed to: 100 g on the unit and its plugs, 235 N, in each of the six directions, held still. It is the peak
   CASE-MARGINS.md already assumes for the face under TEST-PLAN E1 (INFERRED: E1 sets 26 drops from 1.22 m, not a peak), not a measured one.
   Material: Prusament PC Blend (TDS v1.1): interlayer 19, flexural 87, tensile 62 MPa taken (typical less spread); printed
   floor down (the frame flat), 100 percent infill, 0.20 mm layers as the sheet's specimens; walls and posts vertical, so their tension
   crosses the layers, and the frame's bending lies in its layers. Heat deflection 113 C at 0.45 MPa and 93 C at 1.80 MPa, over E3-S's +71 C.
   dir  link                                                                                                                    N       g  factor
   out  frame, back ledge bending at the wall's inner face (93.0 long, lever 2.70)                                           8990    3820    38.2  half the load on each side
   out  frame, back rail bending between its screws and its ledge (arm 10.7, 27.1 wide at each of 3 screws)                  1983     843     8.4  half the load on each side
   out  back frame screws, 3, each holding 1019 N and prised by 3.67 on the post's outer edge                                1664     707     7.1  half the load on each side
   out  frame, knob-edge ledge bending at the wall's inner face (33.0 long, lever 2.20)                                      3915    1663    16.6  half the load on each side
   out  frame, knob-edge rail bending between its screws and its ledge (arm 10.2, 26.1 wide at each of 3 screws)             2004     851     8.5  half the load on each side
   out  knob-edge frame screws, 3, each holding 1019 N and prised by 3.55 on the post's outer edge                           1723     732     7.3  half the load on each side
   out  M3 threads in the lid plate, the four screws between the posts (in 1.4, tip 0.6 short of the bond)                   3958    1682    16.8  INFERRED shear; the six end screws not counted
   out  countersunk heads pulling through the 3.6 flange, the same four                                                      6544    2781    27.8  
   out  tray flange bending between a post and the screw beside it (8.0 x 3.6, arm 5.25), eight places                       2291     973     9.7  the floor not counted
   out* the lid plate's DP8005 bond on polypropylene: SCOPING ONLY (T-peel of 0.5 mm HDPE x perimeter 389)                    613     168          no held figure bounds it
   x    the left panel's bottom band bearing on its sill (1.1 x 61.0 at the loose corner)                                    4160    1768    17.7  
   x    the right panel's bottom band bearing on its sill (1.1 x 38.9 at the loose corner)                                   2653    1127    11.3  the sill cut away under the RF jack
   x    the hinge-end sill sheared off the floor (8.0 x 52.3)                                                                3975    1689    16.9  INFERRED shear
   x    ten M3 through the flanges and both sills, bearing on the printed holes over 3.6                                     6696    2845    28.5  friction not counted
   y    one wall pushed outward, bending across the layers at its root (load 13.0 above it, 4.5 post pitches)                2635    1120    11.2  the frame's tie not counted
   one frame screw holds the least of:
       1019 N  the button head bearing on the 3.0 frame
       1313 N  the square nut bearing on its slot's 3.0 roof
       1520 N  the post and wall at the slot, in tension across the layers (80 mm2)
       2264 N  the screw, A2-70 (INFERRED class)
   Governing link on the makers' typical figures: 707 g, 7.1 times the load case (direction out: back frame screws).
   The bond is not bounded by any held figure: its T-peel scoping number (168 g) is for a flexible strip, not a rigid 2 mm plate, and is
   no bound; it goes to CASE-MARGINS T8 as a pull test on the case's polypropylene, after a thermal cycle (the plate and the lid expand
   differently between -33 and +71 C, and no expansion figure of Peli's polypropylene is held). Nor does PC Blend's sheet state one, so
   the printed tray on its aluminium plate is looked at after E3-S and E4-S as well (cracks at the ten screws, the frame flat).
   TIGHTENING: 0.25 N m on all sixteen M3 (INFERRED; nut factor 0.2): 417 N in a screw, 42 % of what 1.4 mm of thread in the plate strips at
   (990 N, INFERRED shear) and 41 % of what a button head bears on the frame; the r1 row's 0.4 N m would put 667 N, 67 % of the thread.
   SUSTAINED: the pads' preload bends the frame's ledges all the time, +71 C storage included: 0.0222 MPa at the knob-edge ledges' root per
   newton of preload, so 0.45 to 1.17 MPa at the sheet's 25 % figures, and the preload would have to reach 20 N to load the root to the
   0.45 MPa of the sheet's 113 C heat deflection figure, 81 N for the 1.80 MPa of its 93 C figure. Both figures are over +71 C. The
   preload at the nominal 34 % and the most 51 % compression is higher than at 25 % and not stated, so the stress there is not bounded:
   OPEN, read after E3-S (the frame flat on the wall tops, the unit still clamped) and by T9.
   E2 (MIL-STD-810H 514.8 Annex C, composite wheeled vehicle, 40 minutes an axis in the standard, 1 hour in TEST-PLAN): 2.24 g rms in the
   envelope for an unknown orientation, 6.72 g at the 3 sigma the standard limits the drive to, AT THE CASE. The pads' preload keeps the unit
   against the ledges up to 8.6 to 22.4 g (the sheet's 25 % figures over 2.35 N per g), so it stays seated if the lid passes the case's
   vibration on magnified by less than 1.3 to 3.3. The lid's own response is not known: OPEN, read in E2 (the unit is looked at for
   fretting on its top face's edges, the six frame screws and the ten tray screws for loosening). A unit that leaves the ledges for an
   instant is still held: it moves 0.9 at most toward the lid, onto the pads and then the floor.
   E1's peak on the lid is not stated by MIL-STD-810H (it sets the drop, not a pulse). Half-sine from 1.22 m over a stopping distance s:
   s  2.0 mm:  958 g;  s  5.0 mm:  383 g;  s 10.0 mm:  192 g;  s 20.0 mm:   96 g
   The known links hold to 707 g, which that bound passes for s >= 2.7 mm and fails below: a bound that includes failure. No board,
   interface or purchase depends on it (the remedy, the same parts machined in 6061 or a larger bonded plate, moves no board), so the
   retention is DESIGNED to the load case above and its verdict against E1 stays OPEN, allocated to E1 with an accelerometer on the lid
   and to T8 for the bond.

E. THE FITTING. The unit is taken at its largest: the body 0.2 larger on each overall dimension (the maker states no tolerance, INFERRED),
   and everything that stands proud of it 0.5 wider and further out: the knobs d 18.0 and 11.6 high, the button actuators d 4.3 and 2.0 high, the
   RF jack's nut 16.5 across corners with its barrel 14 out of the right panel, the 3.5 mm jacks' bushings d 8.0 and 3.0 out (all INFERRED from
   the maker's photographs; the encoder shafts d 6.0 stand inside the knobs); the panel screws are countersunk and the four feet are NOT fitted.
   Each moving item is taken with every place it passes through on a straight way in; a designed contact (the unit on the floor's stop,
   the frame on the wall tops and on the unit's top face) may touch and may not overlap; everything else keeps 0.20, the printed parts' own
   tolerance.
